---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import dashboardRepair from '@/assets/car-dashboard-leather-repair.webp';
import dashboardProcess from '@/assets/dashboard-process.webp';
import whyChoose from '@/assets/why-choose-dashboard-repair.webp';
import beforeAfter from '@/assets/before-after-dashboard.webp';
import beforeAfter2 from '@/assets/before-after-dashboard-2.webp';
import processDashboard1 from '@/assets/process-dashboard-repair-1.webp';
import processDashboard2 from '@/assets/process-dashboard-repair-2.webp';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Car Dashboard Leather Repair Singapore | Five Star Auto Leather</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Cracked, peeling, or sun-damaged dashboard? We provide professional car dashboard leather repair and reupholstery services in Singapore. Book now!"
    />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-1">
      <Image
        src={dashboardRepair}
        alt="Honda Stepwagon Spada dashboard finished with two-tone black and blue car dashboard leather repair"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[800]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center justify-center bg-black px-4 py-8 sm:order-2 sm:px-16">
      <div
        class="title-slide-up flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-center sm:items-start sm:text-left"
      >
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white">
          Professional Car Dashboard Leather Repair in Singapore
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-8 text-white">
          Your car's dashboard takes the most abuse from Singapore's tropical sun. UV rays, heat and
          humidity cause leather to crack, fade, bubble or peel over time. Whether you drive a
          family MPV, a luxury sedan, or a commercial vehicle, Five Star Auto Leather specialises in
          restoring dashboards to showroom quality. For car dashboard leather repair in Singapore,
          we fully reupholster dashboards using premium materials matched to your vehicle.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-white">
          A damaged dashboard doesn't just look bad. It can also reduce your car's resale value
          significantly.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-white">The good news? We have the solution to your problem.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex w-full items-center justify-start">
          <p class="text-white">
            Call us: <a class="text-white" href="tel:+6591729570">9172 9570</a> / <a
              class="text-white"
              href="tel:+6587909677">8790 9677</a
            >
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.google.com/maps?cid%3D13495479379412370960&sa=D&source=docs&ust=1791519513725617&usg=AOvVaw3feMWT8gvn6GVFGqp0GWgn"
            class="ml-6 inline-block w-50 rounded bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 text-center text-sm font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-red-600"
          >
            Visit our workshop
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
    <div class="flex w-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6">
      <h2 class="mb-0 text-2xl font-bold">The Problem: Why Dashboards Deteriorate</h2>
      <p>
        Singapore's tropical climate is harsh on interior materials. Here's what typically happens:
      </p>
      <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-gray-100">
            <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Symptom</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Cause</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Cracking on the top surface</td>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
              >Prolonged UV exposure hardens and shrinks the leather or PVC surface</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Bubbling or peeling near the windscreen</td
            >
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
              >Heat causes adhesive to fail, especially on afternoon-facing dashboards</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Fading or discolouration</td>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
              >Sunlight bleaches dyes unevenly, leaving patchy colour</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Sticky or gummy surface</td>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
              >Lower-quality dashboard materials degrading in heat</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Curling edges near window seals</td>
            <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Thermal expansion over time</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Most factory dashboards use a thin layer of leather or PVC bonded over foam. That foam
        breaks down in 5 to 8 years depending on sun exposure. All these issues are fixable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-1 sm:col-span-6">
      <Image
        src={dashboardProcess}
        alt="Specialist installing a newly wrapped Hyundai i30 dashboard back onto the vehicle frame during car dashboard leather repair"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center px-4 py-14 sm:order-2 sm:col-span-6 sm:px-6 md:px-20">
      <div class="flex h-full flex-col justify-center">
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-left text-2xl font-bold">Our Dashboard Restoration Process</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Our car dashboard leather repair process is handled entirely in-house, from removal and
          preparation to the final quality check. Watch how a full rewrap is done at Five Star Auto
          Leather.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 1: Free Assessment & Quote</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Bring your vehicle in for a complimentary dashboard assessment. Our specialists will
          inspect your dashboard's condition and provide a customised quotation based on its
          material, damage severity, and the complexity of dismantling and reinstallation.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 2: Surface Preparation</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Before rewrapping, the dashboard is thoroughly cleaned and degreased so the new material
          adheres properly. Worn, peeling or damaged areas are carefully sanded and prepared. Where
          necessary, cracks and deeper imperfections are repaired using a specialised filler
          compound to create a smooth, even surface.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 3: Precision Rewrap</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Using high-temperature resistant and formaldehyde-free industrial adhesives designed for
          Singapore's tropical climate, we apply the new material carefully for a smooth,
          wrinkle-free finish. Every section is carefully bonded to eliminate bubbles, ripples and
          lifting.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 4: Reassembly & Quality Check</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Once the rewrap is complete, all air vents, buttons, trim pieces and sensors are carefully
          reinstalled. We carry out a full quality inspection covering fitment, alignment, finish
          and colour consistency before handing the vehicle back to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Typical turnaround:</strong> 2–3 working days, depending on the extent of damage and
          the complexity of dashboard removal and reinstallation
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-14">
    <div class="grid w-full grid-cols-2 gap-4 px-4 py-8">
      <div class="order-1">
        <Image
          src={processDashboard1}
          alt="Fully dismantled Hyundai dashboard and centre console exposed for car dashboard leather repair"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="order-2">
        <Image
          src={processDashboard2}
          alt="Technician's hands fitting control buttons into a freshly wrapped suede-textured dashboard during car dashboard leather repair"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          widths={[640, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
          class="h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-2 sm:col-span-6">
      <Image
        src={whyChoose}
        alt="Toyota Corolla Cross interior with car dashboard leather repair in rich caramel, complemented by matching front seat car upholstery"
        loading="lazy"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="custom-featured-2 h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center px-4 py-14 sm:order-1 sm:col-span-6 sm:px-6 md:px-20">
      <div
        class="title-slide-up flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-center sm:items-start sm:text-left"
      >
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">Why Choose Five Star Auto Leather?</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Choosing the right specialist for car dashboard leather repair means looking at how a
          workshop prices its work, manages your car's downtime, sources its materials, and controls
          quality. Five Star Auto Leather does all of this in-house.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Transparent Pricing</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Every dashboard rewrap is individually quoted based on your vehicle model, dashboard
          condition, chosen material and the complexity of the work involved. No misleading "from"
          prices or hidden charges — just fair, transparent pricing tailored to your vehicle.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Minimising Downtime</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Dashboard rewrapping is one of the more labour-intensive interior restoration jobs and
          typically takes 2–3 working days (longer for certain luxury and supercar models). If
          you're also reupholstering your seats, steering wheel or other interior components, we'll
          complete everything together whenever possible to minimise your vehicle's downtime.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Built for Singapore's Climate</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We use premium automotive upholstery materials that are heat and UV resistant, paired with
          high-performance adhesives where required. Designed to withstand Singapore's tropical
          climate, your newly rewrapped dashboard is built to maintain its appearance and durability
          for years to come.
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">100% In-House Craftsmanship</h3>
        <p>
          Every dashboard is rewrapped by our experienced craftsmen at our Singapore workshop —
          never outsourced. From careful preparation and precision rewrap to final installation, we
          maintain complete quality control and back our work with a workmanship warranty for your
          peace of mind.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
    <div class="flex w-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6">
      <h2 class="mb-0 text-2xl font-bold">Before & After</h2>
      <p class="mb-4 text-center">
        Every dashboard restoration is a full rewrap job carried out inside our Singapore workshop.
        Here are a few recent examples of what a proper car dashboard leather repair looks like from
        start to finish.
      </p>
      <div class="grid w-full grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="order-1">
          <Image
            src={beforeAfter}
            alt="BMW 630i dashboard before and after car dashboard leather repair, showing removal of cracked red leather and installation of a fresh black suede-textured finish"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
            widths={[640, 1280]}
            sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
            class="mx-auto object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="order-2">
          <Image
            src={beforeAfter2}
            alt="Hyundai i30 dashboard before and after car dashboard leather repair, transforming a cracked factory finish into a premium black suede-textured surface"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
            widths={[640, 1280]}
            sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
            class="mx-auto object-cover"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="w-full bg-black px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <div class="container mx-auto flex max-w-5xl flex-col justify-center gap-6">
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-center text-2xl font-bold text-white">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
        Do you have to remove the entire dashboard to rewrap it?
      </h3>
      <p class="text-white">
        Yes, in most cases. Removing the dashboard allows us to properly prepare the surface and
        wrap it seamlessly around edges and contours, resulting in a much cleaner, longer-lasting
        finish. This is also why dashboard rewrapping is one of the most labour-intensive interior
        upholstery services.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-8 text-white">
        For certain vehicles where only a removable trim section is damaged, we may only need to
        remove that specific panel instead of the entire dashboard.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">How long does dashboard rewrapping take?</h3>
      <p class="mb-8 text-white">
        Most dashboard rewraps take 2–3 working days. Luxury vehicles, supercars and models with
        more complex dashboard designs may require additional time due to the greater dismantling
        complexity and more intricate craftsmanship involved.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Will the new dashboard match my original colour?</h3>
      <p class="mb-8 text-white">
        We aim to achieve the closest possible match using our extensive range of automotive
        upholstery materials and colours. While we cannot always guarantee an exact factory match,
        we can usually achieve a finish that closely resembles your original interior.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Can I change my dashboard to a different colour?</h3>
      <p class="text-white">
        Absolutely. Dashboard rewrapping gives you the freedom to customise your interior to match
        your seats, steering wheel, door panels or your personal style.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-8 text-white">
        However, because the dashboard sits directly beneath the windscreen, we generally recommend
        darker or more muted colours to minimise reflections and glare while driving.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
        Is dashboard rewrapping cheaper than replacing the dashboard?
      </h3>
      <p class="text-white">Not necessarily. The answer depends on your vehicle.</p>
      <p class="text-white">
        Dashboard rewrapping is a highly labour-intensive process involving dismantling, surface
        preparation, template making, upholstery fabrication, stitching, wrapping and
        reinstallation. For some vehicles, especially where replacement dashboards are readily
        available, replacement may cost a similar amount or even less.
      </p>
      <p class="text-white">
        However, for many premium, older or discontinued models where replacement dashboards are
        expensive or difficult to source, rewrapping can be the more practical and cost-effective
        option. During our assessment, we'll be happy to advise which solution makes the most sense
        for your vehicle.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <iframe
    src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3988.6660102489027!2d103.8690919!3d1.3770706000000001!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x31da1658b06d3b7d%3A0xbb4992fe537bc610!2sFive%20Star%20Auto%20Leather!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sph!4v1782371450352!5m2!1sen!2sph"
    width="100%"
    height="450"
    style="border:0;"
    allowfullscreen=""
    loading="lazy"
    referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"></iframe>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-family: 'RacingSansOne', var(--font-sans);
  }
  .custom-featured {
    max-height: 800px;
    object-position: center;
  }
  .custom-featured-2 {
    max-height: 900px;
  }
  .grid-cols-2 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
</style>
